{
  "text": " Hi, my name is Sujata Gibson. I am a civil rights attorney in Ithaca, New York, the principal attorney at the Gibson law firm, and I teach part-time at Cornell Law School in the area of civil rights and movement law. I will be presenting on the civil rights panel and also presenting a keynote speech at the conference on the role of movement lawyers in this pandemic litigation. This pandemic has been used to grab unprecedented powers and has resulted in widespread erosion of our most basic civil rights, human rights, and constitutional freedoms. It is vital that all of us movement lawyers, all of us lawyers who care and see what's going on communicate with one another and get together to really understand what we're doing here to support this movement and to take back our democracy and ensure that our most basic rights are not run roughshod and do not get lost forever. We need more attorneys. There's a lot of cases out there and we need help. So if you are considering doing this kind of litigation and it's vital that you come and that we get to meet you and you get to meet us, I think there's some great presenters at this conference and I'm really looking forward to meeting you all.",
